hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2701","\nNarrated to us Bundār, narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar, narrated to us Shuʿbah, from Salamah (who is Ibn Kuhayl), who said: I heard Muslim al-Baṭīn, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās (RA), who said:\n\During the pre-Islamic period"","" a woman would perform Tawāf around the House (Kaʿbah) while naked"","" saying: 'Today"","" part of him or all of him will be revealed. So whatever part of him is revealed"","" I will not make it permissible (for myself).'\nThen the verse was revealed:\n' O children of Adam"","" take your adornment at every masjid...' (Qur’ān 7:31).\"""""""
"2702","\nNarrated to us ‘Īsā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ghāfiqī:\nOn the authority of Ibn Wahb, from Yūnus ibn Yazīd and ‘Amr ibn al-Ḥārith, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sa‘īd ibn al-Musayyib, that he used to say:\n*\The Day of Sacrifice is the Day of the Greatest Hajj.\""*\n\nIbn Shihāb said"","" narrated to us from Ḥumayd ibn ‘Abd al-Raḥmān ibn ‘Awf"","" from Abū Hurayrah (RA)"","" that he said:\n*\""Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (RA) sent me during the Hajj in which the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) appointed him as commander before the Farewell Hajj"","" with a group of people. They were to announce to the people on the Day of Sacrifice: ‘No polytheist shall perform Hajj after this day"","" and no naked person shall perform Tawāf around the House.’\""*\n\nIbn Shihāb said"","" and Ḥumayd used to say:\n*\""The Day of Sacrifice is the Day of the Greatest Hajj"",""\""* because of the hadith of Abū Hurayrah (RA)."""""
